WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.990
On the US High Plains, many farms
water their crops from below.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.030
Wells pump it up from an
aquifer: rock that stores water.

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.230
This aquifer lies under
parts of eight states:

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.890
about 453,000 square kilometres.

5
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:19.570
Large-scale irrigation began around 1950.

6
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:24.990
In 2015, about 95 per cent of the
water pumped went to irrigation.

7
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:29.110
So what happens when farms take
out more than the rain puts back?

8
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.170
In this mission, you'll
see how rock stores water,

9
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.290
and how wells reach it.

10
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.230
Then you'll weigh three possible
futures for the High Plains.

11
00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.850
Your mission: find out what happens when
farms pump out more water than the rain

12
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:43.890
puts back.
